(e) Promotion and protection of human rights, including monitoring, investigating, and reporting on violations and abuses of human rights and international humanitarian law, and supporting efforts to end impunity;

6. Further decides that MINUSCA shall carry out the following additional tasks:
(a) Support for the extension of State authority, the deployment of civil administration, and the reform of the security sector (SSR), including by assisting in the capacity-building of the Central African Armed Forces (FACA) and internal security forces, in close coordination and partnership with the CAR authorities while fully respecting the national ownership and leadership of the CAR Government, and with international partners;
(b) Support for disarmament, demobilization, reintegration (DDR), and community violence reduction (CVR) programs, as well as repatriation of foreign combatants;
(c) Support for national and international justice, the fight against impunity, and the rule of law, including continued technical and operational support to the Special Criminal Court;
(d) Assistance to the CAR authorities in preventing and countering the illicit proliferation and trafficking of small arms, light weapons, and the illicit exploitation of natural resources;
(e) Support for mine-action activities, explosive ordnance risk education, and the mitigation of threats posed by explosive devices, and calls on the Secretariat and international partners to ensure MINUSCA is provided with adequate resources, training, and capabilities, particularly for counter-IED and explosive ordnance disposal, to guarantee peacekeeper safety and security;

7. Reaffirms the importance of MINUSCA’s freedom of movement, unhindered operational capability, including unhindered aerial operations, and full compliance with the Status of Forces Agreement (SOFA), urges the CAR authorities to ensure the safety, security, and unimpeded access of MINUSCA personnel throughout the territory, including by lifting all remaining restrictions on MINUSCA's aerial operations, notably night flights and uncrewed aerial systems, and emphasizes the importance of continuous dialogue, enhanced coordination, and mutual trust between MINUSCA and the CAR authorities in mandate implementation;

8. Calls upon the CAR Government and regional partners to intensify cross-border cooperation to enhance border security, stem the illicit flow of arms and fighters, and mitigate the humanitarian and security impacts of the crisis in the Sudan, and calls upon the international community to mobilize increased humanitarian and financial support to assist the CAR in addressing the spillover effects of regional instability;

9. Requests the Secretary-General to report to the Security Council on the situation in the CAR and the implementation of MINUSCA’s mandate by 15 February 2026, 15 June 2026, and 15 October 2026;

10. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

